# Mossy ruins: a meadow, a blob47-round family (rounder inner corners, since G9) of grass on sand, for the village above the
# beach. Route 1: the textures are the grass tile (inside) and the sand tile (outside); from the
# sand in, 2 px of sand, a dark rim of moss, then the grass. Tufts reach over the rim on the three
# pieces, so the edge reads as grass growing out into the sand, not a cut line.
new family meadow 24x24 scheme=blob47-round palette=ruins-shore
family texture inside from=grass
family texture outside from=sand
family band 2:outside 1:moss1 radius=3 fillet=10

# --- tufts over the rim (ew: north and south edges; ns: west and east; o: the outer corners)
px @cell(ew) 5,1 6,1 15,1 9,22 18,22 19,22 c=moss2
px @cell(ew) 5,0 15,0 c=moss1
px @cell(ew) 9,23 19,23 c=moss1
px @cell(ns) 1,4 1,15 22,7 22,18 c=moss2
px @cell(ns) 0,4 0,15 23,7 23,18 c=moss1
px @cell(o) 6,2 2,17 21,6 17,21 c=moss2
